    "user": {
      "login": "mfreed7",
      "id": 29559695,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjI5NTU5Njk1",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29559695?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/mfreed7",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/mfreed7",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mfreed7/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mfreed7/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mfreed7/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mfreed7/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mfreed7/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mfreed7/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mfreed7/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mfreed7/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mfreed7/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "Well, it's a [standard from 1999](https://www.w3.org/TR/xslt-10/), which has been superseded by [two new major releases](https://www.w3.org/TR/xslt/) ([2.0 in 2009](https://www.w3.org/TR/2009/PER-xslt20-20090421/), and [3.0 in 2017](https://www.w3.org/TR/xslt-30/)) with a [4.0 version in the works since 2020](https://archive.xmlprague.cz/2020/files/xmlprague-2020-proceedings.pdf#page=121). Browsers, to my knowledge, only implement version 1.0, from 27 years ago. So at least in my personal view, we're decades behind the latest standard.\r\n\r\nHaving said all of that, I really don't mind changing the language completely - just let me know what you'd be comfortable saying. I can even go back to just saying \"it's deprecated\" without the reason. But the other example @zcorpan [pointed me to](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12805#issuecomment-5368161294) included a motivation, so I was just trying to follow that pattern.\r\n",
    "created_at": "2026-08-24T21:10:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-24T21:10:42Z",
